newline
[-]++++++++++.
[-]

<<<+                    move to t0 set run flag to 1
[
    prompt
>[-]            move to t1 and zero it

+++++           set t1 to 5 and adds 8 to t2 5 times (need 37 for a % sign)
[>++++++++<-]   

>---.           move to t2 makes it 37 and prints
-----.          subtract 5 to make it 32 and a space         ends on t2
    [-]                 clear t2
    <,                  move to t1 read letter into it
    >,[-]               move to t2 spit out and eat extra character (TODO: maybe not a good thing?)
    >                   back home!!! t3


    e is echo
    q is quit
    r is read
    w is write

    WE KEEP SUBTRACTING UNTIL WE HIT ZERO AND THEN THATS A MATCH (REMEMBER SQUARE BRACKETS RUN IF 0)

    start with highest ascii (e)
    <<-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    [>+>+<<-]           empty out t1 into both t2 and t3 (classic loop pretty easy to understand)
    >>[<<+>>-]          empty t3 back into t1
    +<[>-<[-]]>         set t3=1  move to t2  if t2 nonzero then t3 is set to 0 and t2 cleared

    [
        start on t3
<,                  move to t2
----------          subtract 10 (\n in ascii)

We do this to determine if there is data at the cell or if it is a newline and there is nothing to echo!

[                   remember square brackets only run if the cell is nonzero
    ++++++++++      restore the cell to its previous value since it was not indeed a LF
    .               prints
    ,               read next character (the terminal buffers it up we dont have to do that :yay:)
    ----------      same \n logic as before we conclude this iteration of the loop and get taken back to the start
]

++++++++++          prepare the actual newline
.                   print :D
[-]                 loop until the cell is back at 0

>                   move back to t3       hopefully the linker can superposition it here like a #include
        -               erooo it out
    ]

    q
    <<------------      12 more than e (ascii)
    [>+>+<<-]           empty out t1 into both t2 and t3 (classic loop pretty easy to understand)
    >>[<<+>>-]          empty t3 back into t1
    +<[>-<[-]]>         set t3=1  move to t2  if t2 nonzero then t3 is set to 0 and t2 cleared

    [
        <<<[-]>>>       ZERO OUT THE RUN FLAG!!! (quits)
        -
    ]

    r
    <<-                 1 more than q (ascii)
    [>+>+<<-]           empty out t1 into both t2 and t3 (classic loop pretty easy to understand)
    >>[<<+>>-]          empty t3 back into t1
    +<[>-<[-]]>         set t3=1  move to t2  if t2 nonzero then t3 is set to 0 and t2 cleared

    [
        remember we are supposed to start at t3
>>                  now at t5 the start of the buffer
[.>]                read then next cell  repeats until 0 (aka buffer terminator)
<[<]                slide back to guard (t4)
++++++++++.         make guard 10 and print (for a newline)
[-]                 set guard to 0
<                   back to t3
        -
    ]

    w
    119 minus 114=5
    <<-----
    [>+>+<<-]           empty out t1 into both t2 and t3 (classic loop pretty easy to understand)
    >>[<<+>>-]          empty t3 back into t1
    +<[>-<[-]]>         set t3=1  move to t2  if t2 nonzero then t3 is set to 0 and t2 cleared
    
    [
        remember we are supposed to start at t3
>>                  at t5 aka start of buffer
,----------         read remove 10 (newline trick)
[                   loop while not newline (remember 10 (newline) minus 10 is 0 and that terminates a loop)
    ++++++++++      restore character
    >               next buffer cell
    ,----------     same old minus 10 trick
]
<[<]                slide over to guard cell
<                   back to t3
        -
    ]
    <<<                 (to check the run flag)
]   
